   "id": "eruvin.55b.7",
   "daf": "55b",
   "sentenceId": 6,
   "he": "הָיוּ שָׁם גְּדוּדִיּוֹת גְּבוֹהוֹת עֲשָׂרָה טְפָחִים כּוּ׳. מַאי גְּדוּדִיּוֹת? אָמַר רַב יְהוּדָה: שָׁלֹשׁ מְחִיצּוֹת שֶׁאֵין עֲלֵיהֶן תִּקְרָה.",
   "en": "We learned in the mishna: If «there were remnants» of walls «ten handbreadths high» on the outskirts of a city, they are considered part of the city, and the Shabbat limit is measured from them. The Gemara asks: «What are» these «remnants? Rav Yehuda said: Three partitions that do not have a roof over them,» which are considered part of the city despite the fact that they do not comprise a proper house."
  }
